{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"desirable-marshy-zeren","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# A stranded local refs/reconciler/lock wedges every local reconcile pass permanently\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nLocal `rebar reconcile` repeatedly fails with `reconcile: refs/reconciler/lock held by a live pass — yielding` (exit 3) even when the authoritative remote holds no lock and no holder process exists anywhere. Recovery required a manual `git update-ref -d refs/reconciler/lock`, and the condition kept recurring.\n\nProven mechanism, reproduced end-to-end in a clean sandbox (real bare remote + working clone, real `_ref_lock` primitives, no mocks):\n\n1. The GitHub Actions bridge acquires the lock on the remote (it holds/heartbeats it near-continuously: `git ls-remote origin refs/reconciler/lock` returns a DIFFERENT oid on successive samples).\n2. Any local pass calls `read(..., remote=\"origin\")`. `_fetch_ref` (`_ref_lock.py:288-293`) runs `git fetch origin +<ref>:<ref>`, which PLANTS a local copy of the bridge's lock.\n3. The bridge releases. `release` in remote mode (`_ref_lock.py:381-406`) pushes a delete to the REMOTE ONLY and never touches the local ref, so the local copy is STRANDED: remote free, local still held.\n4. Every later local `read` reports `HELD holder=GHA-bridge` while the remote is free, because `_ref_oid` (`:301-315`) force-fetches and then falls back to `rev-parse` on the surviving local ref. Git cannot delete a local ref via a refspec whose source is absent, so the fetch failing (`fatal: couldn't find remote ref`, exit 128) leaves the orphan intact — contrary to `_fetch_ref`'s own comment claiming it \"becomes absent locally = free\".\n5. `steal()` cannot break it either: `--force-with-lease` against an absent remote ref is rejected as `stale info`, which `_PUSH_REJECT_MARKERS` (`:619`) classifies as a CAS mismatch, logged misleadingly as \"CAS lost to another contender\". Measured: `steal(...)` returns None with the orphan intact.\n\nNet effect: the checkout is wedged FOREVER and manual break-glass is the only escape.\n\n## Why this is a defect (authority)\n\n`docs/adr/0031-reconciler-ref-lock.md` §\"Distributed operation\": \"The lock must be authoritative across CI runners, manual invocations, and clones\" and with `remote=\"origin\"` \"the remote is the truth\". A stranded local ref overriding a free remote violates that invariant directly.\n\nSame ADR §\"Operator break-glass\": \"C2's relative-duration lease makes this rarely necessary — a crashed holder's lock becomes steal-able after one lease interval automatically.\" Here it is NEVER steal-able and break-glass is ALWAYS required. The ADR also names both halves of a clear (`git push origin :refs/reconciler/lock` AND `git update-ref -d refs/reconciler/lock`), showing the design knows the local ref is a separate artifact the release path must handle.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- After a remote holder acquires, a local pass reads, and the remote holder releases, a later local `read(..., remote=\"origin\")` reports the lock FREE (not HELD).\n- `release(..., remote=\"origin\")` leaves no local `refs/reconciler/lock` behind.\n- A stranded local ref is reclaimable without manual intervention — either it reads free, or `steal()` breaks it.\n- A GENUINELY live remote holder still reads as HELD, so cross-machine mutual exclusion is preserved (the fix must not make every lock look free).\n- No local pass source is introduced or required: the Reconciler Bridge runs on GitHub Actions only.\n\n## Ruled out during investigation\n\n- The steal kill-switch: `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_STEAL` defaults ON (`__main__.py:170-184`) and is unset locally; driving `steal_pass_lock` directly DID break a stale lease (fence 2 -> 3). Stealing is not disabled.\n- A hidden local scheduler: no git hook, LaunchAgent (only a build updater + worktree GC), crontab, MCP tool, or implicit CLI path runs a reconcile pass. Operator-run local passes plus this bug fully explain recurrence.\n- `_advisory_lock.py`'s fail-closed swallow: no exception is raised; `steal()` returns None cleanly.","id":"a4b2-67bb-1bb0-484f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Stranded local refs/reconciler/lock wedges every local reconcile pass permanently"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785218397704890001,"uuid":"e73016ef-0938-47a6-be2e-c9f802ad431a"}